   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Contour/WindingInteger.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `h_a_ne` from the signature and derive it internally, e.g. `have h_a_ne : \u03b3 a - w \u2260 0 := fun h => Complex.slitPlane_ne_zero (h_slit a \u27e8le_rfl, hab\u27e9) (by rw [h, zero_div])`.",
   "issue": "`segment_log_FTC` takes `h_a_ne : \u03b3 a - w \u2260 0` as a separate hypothesis, but it is implied by `h_slit`: `h_slit a \u27e8le_rfl, hab\u27e9` gives `(\u03b3 a - w)/(\u03b3 a - w) \u2208 slitPlane`, and `slitPlane_ne_zero` forces `(\u03b3 a - w)/(\u03b3 a - w) \u2260 0` (else `0/0 = 0 \u2209 slitPlane`), hence `\u03b3 a - w \u2260 0`. The extra assumption is stronger than necessary.",
